0..76 Comment "//! A case on a vector checks each arm at the fields of its own constructor."
77..80 Comment "//!"
81..159 Comment "//! A case on an indexed family works as a case on a family with no indices. A"
160..229 Comment "//! case may still write an arm whose constructor cannot stand at the"
230..309 Comment "//! scrutinee\'s index, as `oneLength` does. `vector-head.gandr` leaves that arm"
310..318 Comment "//! out."
319..322 Comment "//!"
323..396 Comment "//! An arm may return a constructor at a length that a call computes. The"
397..470 Comment "//! `VCons` arm of `vappend` returns `VCons` at `plus(m, Succ(k))`, which"
471..515 Comment "//! computes the length that `VCons` states."
516..519 Comment "//!"
520..600 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families] — a case that checks each arm at"
601..635 Comment "//!   its own constructor\'s fields"
636..714 Comment "//! - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
715..741 Comment "//!   the length it states"
742..745 Comment "//!"
746..847 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308 \"Dybjer, Inductive families\""
849..886 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
887..893 Keyword "import"
894..895 StringLit "\""
895..912 StringLit "./data-base.gandr"
912..913 StringLit "\""
913..914 Other ";"
